WEBVTT

00:06.631 --> 00:07.799
Get out of here!

00:08.383 --> 00:10.385
I won't give you the key, no matter what!

00:10.468 --> 00:13.221
And I won't tell you how to use it either!

00:14.097 --> 00:17.392
What is happening? Are those two fighting?

00:18.309 --> 00:21.187
What should I do? Eavesdropping is rude.

00:21.688 --> 00:24.524
But if they're fighting,
I should try to stop them.

00:30.697 --> 00:32.157
Stop it!

00:33.199 --> 00:35.702
What are you doing? Let go of him!

00:36.703 --> 00:38.621
You're so noisy.

00:39.539 --> 00:40.707
Who are you?

00:40.790 --> 00:42.500
How could you do that to a child?

00:42.584 --> 00:43.418
Let go of…

00:45.462 --> 00:47.005
He's not even budging.

00:48.173 --> 00:51.426
Even though his arms are thin
and he's smaller than me.

00:52.302 --> 00:53.928
Take your hand off of me.

00:56.181 --> 00:57.599
HYOTTOKO

00:57.682 --> 00:59.267
You are incredibly weak.

00:59.350 --> 01:01.770
I'm surprised you got into the Corps.

01:04.814 --> 01:07.358
I feel something strange
emanating from that box.

01:08.151 --> 01:09.569
Do I sense a demon?

01:10.904 --> 01:13.448
What's inside that box?

01:14.908 --> 01:16.117
Don't you dare touch it!

01:31.633 --> 01:34.469
Demon Slayer:
Swordsmith Village Arc

02:50.628 --> 02:52.964
Episode 2
Yoriichi Type Zero

02:59.304 --> 03:00.388
He took the boy.

03:00.471 --> 03:01.472
Are you all right?

03:02.098 --> 03:03.099
Let go of me!

03:03.182 --> 03:05.602
You're probably dizzy.
That was really dangerous.

03:05.685 --> 03:07.103
Get away from me!

03:07.186 --> 03:11.774
I won't give the key to anyone,
not even if you guys torture me.

03:12.525 --> 03:14.360
It'll definitely break down next time.

03:14.944 --> 03:17.113
Have you been trained
to withstand torture?

03:19.532 --> 03:23.244
Even most adults can't endure it,
let alone a brat like you.

03:23.953 --> 03:26.539
You appear to be
an exceedingly stupid brat.

03:27.832 --> 03:30.877
So what if it does break down?
You could just build it again.

03:31.628 --> 03:33.796
How many people do you think will die

03:33.880 --> 03:38.134
while you're rambling on and on
about such trivial matters?

03:39.719 --> 03:42.972
That's what happens when you get
in the way of a Hashira's duties.

03:43.806 --> 03:47.602
A Hashira's time and your time
have completely different values.

03:48.311 --> 03:51.064
You'd understand that
if you used your head a little.

03:51.147 --> 03:54.943
Swordsmiths can't fight.
You can't save someone's life.

03:55.443 --> 03:57.820
The only thing
you guys can do is make weapons.

03:59.822 --> 04:01.574
So, come on, give me the key.

04:02.325 --> 04:04.953
Act according to your own position.

04:05.620 --> 04:07.247
You are not a baby anymore.

04:11.793 --> 04:13.044
What are you doing?

04:13.670 --> 04:16.256
I just… How do I say it?

04:16.339 --> 04:17.590
I really don't like you!

04:17.674 --> 04:19.717
What is it you lack? Sympathy, maybe?

04:19.801 --> 04:22.595
You're lacking in sympathy
and are just plain cruel!

04:23.179 --> 04:25.932
You think this is cruel? Are you--

04:26.015 --> 04:27.392
I'm not saying you're wrong!

04:27.475 --> 04:30.103
I admit that what you're saying
is basically true,

04:30.603 --> 04:32.647
so you're not technically wrong.

04:32.730 --> 04:36.276
But the swordsmiths' job is also vital.
Their work plays a critical role!

04:39.237 --> 04:42.824
They have incredible skills
that are different from us swordsmen.

04:42.907 --> 04:47.829
In fact, we probably couldn't do anything
without the swords they make for us.

04:49.330 --> 04:53.209
Swordsmen and swordsmiths need each other.

04:53.710 --> 04:55.378
We're all fighting the same battle.

04:55.878 --> 04:58.047
Every day, in our own way,
we all fight to--

04:58.131 --> 04:58.965
Sorry, but…

04:59.966 --> 05:03.803
I don't have time to stand here
and listen to your boring speech.

05:08.641 --> 05:12.353
What do I do? I can't carry him
down the mountain by myself!

05:12.437 --> 05:16.649
Don't worry, I'll carry him.
If he doesn't wake up soon…

05:18.026 --> 05:21.779
His eyelids are fluttering.
He's about to wake up!

05:21.863 --> 05:23.823
-Goodbye!
-Hey!

05:26.576 --> 05:29.537
Are you all right?
You shouldn't get up so quickly.

05:29.620 --> 05:31.164
Was Mr. Haganezuka here?

05:31.789 --> 05:33.583
Wasn't he here just now?

05:33.666 --> 05:36.002
No, he wasn't here.

05:38.546 --> 05:40.381
It must have been my imagination then.

05:41.424 --> 05:42.717
Where's that Hashira?

05:42.800 --> 05:45.344
I gave him the key, so he left.

05:46.054 --> 05:47.764
So you did give it to him?

05:47.847 --> 05:50.141
It did seem like you had no choice.

05:50.224 --> 05:53.186
Well, it's not really my place
to have said anything about it

05:53.269 --> 05:55.354
since I don't know the whole situation.

05:55.438 --> 05:56.689
Hey, don't be like that!

05:57.398 --> 06:01.027
I'm glad that you stood up for me,
even though we're total strangers.

06:01.819 --> 06:03.071
Thank you very much.

06:03.613 --> 06:05.573
No, I wasn't any help at all.

06:07.825 --> 06:10.787
And what about the man
who was standing here?

06:10.870 --> 06:12.622
That was a mechanical doll.

06:13.289 --> 06:14.457
A mechanical doll?

06:15.291 --> 06:17.293
That guy took it with him.

06:18.377 --> 06:21.506
He needed the key
in order to make the doll move.

06:23.174 --> 06:24.926
That doll must be important to you.

06:26.469 --> 06:28.721
But why was a Hashira searching for it?

06:29.263 --> 06:30.807
That one is special.

06:31.808 --> 06:35.603
That mechanical doll
is stronger than a human

06:35.686 --> 06:37.772
and is capable of performing 108 moves,

06:37.855 --> 06:40.066
so it can be used for combat training.

06:41.484 --> 06:42.735
So that's why…

06:42.819 --> 06:45.196
However, that doll has already…

06:48.950 --> 06:49.951
What was that sound?

06:50.034 --> 06:51.661
That guy must be using it.

06:51.744 --> 06:52.829
This way!

07:04.132 --> 07:06.717
It can hold its own
against a Hashira. Amazing.

07:06.801 --> 07:10.430
That's the combat mechanical doll
built by my ancestors,

07:11.055 --> 07:12.765
Yoriichi Type Zero.

07:14.434 --> 07:16.894
But why does it have six?

07:16.978 --> 07:18.187
You mean its arms?

07:18.771 --> 07:24.485
According to my father, that doll was
modeled on an actual swordsman.

07:24.986 --> 07:26.446
He said, the swordman's moves

07:26.529 --> 07:29.740
could not be replicated
unless they gave it six arms.

07:32.243 --> 07:36.581
That face… I feel like I know it,
but I can't remember from where.

07:37.498 --> 07:40.460
Who was that swordsman?
Where was he from and what did he do?

07:40.543 --> 07:43.921
I'm sorry,
but I don't know all the details.

07:44.005 --> 07:45.965
His story is from the Sengoku period.

07:46.048 --> 07:50.261
The Sengoku period?
That was over three centuries ago!

07:50.803 --> 07:52.096
That's what I was told.

07:52.180 --> 07:55.641
And that doll
hasn't broken down in all that time?

07:56.267 --> 07:59.145
It's an amazing technology
we haven't been able to replicate

07:59.228 --> 08:00.062
to this today.

08:01.856 --> 08:04.609
If it's broken,
we won't be able repair it.

08:06.235 --> 08:09.655
My father passed away very suddenly
and I don't have any siblings.

08:09.739 --> 08:12.241
I'm supposed to step up
and take care of it now,

08:12.325 --> 08:15.661
but I have no talent for forging swords
or tinkering with machines.

08:17.288 --> 08:20.500
So, that's why you were so desperate…
I understand now.

08:23.127 --> 08:25.087
That guy's incredible,

08:25.171 --> 08:27.757
even though he doesn't appear
to be older than I am…

08:28.424 --> 08:31.177
But he's a Hashira
and he has a lot of talent.

08:31.260 --> 08:33.054
Of course he does!

08:33.137 --> 08:36.724
He's a descendant of the wielder
of the Sun Breathing style after all!

08:37.517 --> 08:39.268
That boy is a prodigy.

08:39.352 --> 08:41.938
He's on a whole different level
than the likes of you.

08:43.981 --> 08:45.775
Are you Tokito's crow?

08:46.400 --> 08:49.362
And, "Sun Breathing"?
Do you mean the first Breathing Style?

08:50.154 --> 08:52.198
No wonder he's so incredible.

08:54.992 --> 08:57.870
But he's not using
the Sun Breathing style now, is he?

09:00.373 --> 09:03.417
Shut your mouth
or I'll peck your eyeballs out!

09:03.834 --> 09:06.212
Hey, I just remembered! My dream!

09:06.295 --> 09:08.881
I saw that man in a dream!

09:09.757 --> 09:14.637
What? Are you stupid or something?
Have you even been to this village before?

09:14.720 --> 09:17.181
That's so preposterous, I could laugh!

09:17.265 --> 09:20.184
Are you saying you've met
a warrior from the Sengoku period?

09:20.268 --> 09:22.228
How old even are you?

09:23.896 --> 09:27.817
I'm sorry. There's something wrong
with me, isn't there?

09:27.900 --> 09:28.901
That's not true!

09:30.111 --> 09:32.947
Maybe it's an inherited memory?

09:33.030 --> 09:35.658
People in my village often talk about it.

09:35.741 --> 09:38.661
Our ancestors passed on
more than just their appearance.

09:38.744 --> 09:41.497
Living creatures
can pass on memories as well.

09:43.416 --> 09:47.587
What you saw in your dream
must have been your ancestor's memory.

09:47.670 --> 09:50.965
What? That's preposterous!
It doesn't even make any sense!

09:51.882 --> 09:54.093
That's very kind of you, thanks.

09:55.094 --> 09:57.388
I'm Tanjiro. What's your name?

09:57.930 --> 09:59.682
I'm Kotetsu.

09:59.765 --> 10:03.394
Don't pay any attention
to what that mean female crow says.

10:12.069 --> 10:12.945
The armor broke!

10:17.992 --> 10:18.951
Kotetsu!

10:19.035 --> 10:25.833
DEMON SLAYER:
SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC

10:29.045 --> 10:32.131
Kotetsu!

10:32.214 --> 10:35.509
I will find you!
I have a really good sense of smell.

10:36.469 --> 10:38.638
Even though it's not
in great shape right now.

10:39.180 --> 10:41.223
I think he went this way.

10:45.561 --> 10:46.937
Kotetsu!

10:47.021 --> 10:50.066
Is that as high as you can climb?

10:51.609 --> 10:53.944
If there's anything I can do,
I'll help you.

10:54.028 --> 10:56.197
Don't give up on the doll yet.

10:57.531 --> 10:59.283
You still have a long future ahead.

11:01.160 --> 11:02.787
You have to work hard now

11:02.870 --> 11:05.498
so you can be successful
in 10 or 20 years.

11:06.290 --> 11:09.460
Even if you can't do it now,
you'll be able to do it eventually.

11:10.628 --> 11:11.712
No, I won't.

11:12.505 --> 11:15.091
I don't need anybody
to tell me that I'm no good.

11:15.716 --> 11:19.428
Everything's going to end
with my generation and it's all my fault!

11:23.682 --> 11:26.352
You can't give up
and throw away your responsibility.

11:26.435 --> 11:29.271
I wish you wouldn't talk
about yourself that way.

11:30.439 --> 11:33.609
He came up here so silently.
So this is what a swordsman can do.

11:34.193 --> 11:38.447
Even if you can't do it yourself,
someone will definitely take over.

11:39.156 --> 11:41.951
You have to put in the effort
so that it gets passed on.

11:42.451 --> 11:43.661
Even if you can't do it,

11:43.744 --> 11:46.622
maybe your children
or your grandchildren will be able to.

11:47.832 --> 11:51.168
I want to defeat Muzan Kibutsuji.

11:52.086 --> 11:54.922
I want to save my sister,
who's been turned into a demon.

11:56.340 --> 11:58.342
But I may die before I reach my goals.

11:59.718 --> 12:03.472
Still, I have faith that someone else
will finish the job for me.

12:04.390 --> 12:06.600
Just like the baton of life
was passed on to us

12:06.684 --> 12:08.561
so we could defeat an Upper Rank Demon,

12:09.145 --> 12:14.150
the life we pass on
will definitely defeat Kibutsuji one day.

12:18.487 --> 12:19.738
Let's do our best together!

12:21.866 --> 12:22.700
Okay.

12:24.201 --> 12:29.582
I didn't want to see that doll be broken,
but my mind is made up now.

12:30.332 --> 12:32.668
His combat training
should last until nightfall,

12:33.294 --> 12:36.464
so I'll prepare myself to see it through.

12:39.758 --> 12:42.511
Really? So, you're ten years old?

12:42.595 --> 12:43.596
Yes.

12:43.679 --> 12:45.222
My little brother is…

12:47.933 --> 12:50.186
What? You're done already?

12:51.312 --> 12:52.229
Yes, I am.

12:52.897 --> 12:54.607
It was a good training session.

12:55.858 --> 12:56.984
Who are you again?

12:58.527 --> 12:59.445
That's right.

12:59.528 --> 13:01.572
My sword broke…

13:02.531 --> 13:05.075
so I'll be taking this one with me.

13:08.496 --> 13:09.705
Kotetsu!

13:10.706 --> 13:13.000
Dispose of that sword.

13:15.252 --> 13:17.338
I don't smell
any malice emanating from him.

13:17.421 --> 13:19.673
He must not be doing it on purpose.

13:20.549 --> 13:22.259
But still…

13:26.096 --> 13:28.599
I smell a lot of malice
coming from that crow.

13:29.350 --> 13:31.310
She really looks down on me.

13:33.270 --> 13:34.146
Kotetsu!

13:53.249 --> 13:57.461
Kotetsu, let's check if it can still move.

14:10.724 --> 14:13.519
It's not moving. I guess it's already…

14:21.861 --> 14:24.738
All right! It's moving, Kotetsu!

14:24.822 --> 14:26.198
Isn't that… great?

14:28.617 --> 14:30.995
Yes, you're right, Tanjiro.

14:32.413 --> 14:35.499
I want you to train with this doll

14:35.583 --> 14:38.502
and become stronger
than that emotionless jerk!

14:38.586 --> 14:41.589
And I will do my best to help you!

14:44.758 --> 14:45.968
Starting now?

15:01.400 --> 15:04.028
I'm gonna die!
Fighting against six arms is impossible!

15:04.111 --> 15:05.154
It only has five now.

15:05.738 --> 15:09.575
Since that brat broke one off,
it's not at its full potential anymore.

15:11.452 --> 15:14.163
Tanjiro, please, get stronger.

15:14.246 --> 15:16.248
And when you do, tell him this,

15:16.874 --> 15:19.043
"Is that all you've got,
you piece of shit?"

15:20.294 --> 15:24.089
"Your hair is too long.
Get a haircut, seaweed head!"

15:24.173 --> 15:26.842
"Pissant! You ugly little midget!"

15:26.926 --> 15:29.178
"Kill yourself, you shameless jerk!"

15:30.137 --> 15:33.849
Wait, Kotetsu! That's going way too far!

15:33.933 --> 15:36.268
Would beheading him be better?

15:36.352 --> 15:38.646
No! I just can't say
those kinds of things!

15:38.729 --> 15:40.856
-You will tell him!
-No!

15:40.940 --> 15:43.484
You have to tell him. Please!

15:49.406 --> 15:52.785
Even if I didn't want to admit it,
Tokito was really incredible.

15:53.452 --> 15:56.330
Despite being smaller
and younger than I am.

15:57.206 --> 16:01.835
I won't lose to him.
I have to get a lot stronger.

16:11.595 --> 16:15.432
Tanjiro! You're worthless
if that's all it takes to kill you!

16:15.516 --> 16:18.811
Keep working at it. I'll say it again,
so get up and look at me!

16:22.231 --> 16:24.233
You're moving
solely out of habit, Tanjiro.

16:24.316 --> 16:25.401
Don't you understand?

16:26.986 --> 16:30.531
You don't decide how to move
after observing your opponent's moves.

16:30.614 --> 16:31.949
That's why you're no good!

16:32.032 --> 16:34.994
Do you understand now?
You don't even have the basics down.

16:35.077 --> 16:38.122
I'm even surprised
you survived this long in the Corps.

16:38.205 --> 16:40.290
Everything you do
is just barely acceptable.

16:40.374 --> 16:43.460
I'm gonna beat that weaknesses out of you.

16:43.544 --> 16:47.256
I won't give you any food
until you can do exactly what I tell you!

16:49.717 --> 16:50.551
Okay.

16:54.471 --> 16:57.641
Tanjiro, you're too slow!
That's no good at all!

16:57.725 --> 17:00.894
You'd be dead
if the doll wasn't using practice sticks.

17:00.978 --> 17:02.062
Get it together!

17:02.604 --> 17:07.192
Today is day five. Starting tomorrow,
I'm giving the doll real swords.

17:07.901 --> 17:10.738
Wait, even with the practice sticks
it's almost killing me.

17:10.821 --> 17:12.614
I'm going to die!

17:14.658 --> 17:16.452
No food again today!

17:18.620 --> 17:21.290
Kotetsu has an impressive talent
for analysis.

17:21.373 --> 17:22.291
Come on, get up!

17:22.374 --> 17:25.127
But as a swordsmanship instructor,
he's a total amateur.

17:25.210 --> 17:26.795
-I need a break.
-Come on!

17:26.879 --> 17:29.089
He doesn't know
the limits of the human body,

17:29.173 --> 17:31.216
so his training sessions are brutal.

17:31.300 --> 17:36.555
If I can't follow his instructions,
he'll give me absolutely no food or water.

17:36.638 --> 17:40.601
Without any water,
a human would die in three or so days.

17:42.394 --> 17:43.812
UNCLOUDED EYES

17:44.605 --> 17:47.566
This is pure tyranny
born out of ignorance.

17:49.568 --> 17:52.905
In the midst of the training,
my life was saved by the rain.

17:54.990 --> 17:57.910
During horrendous physical exertion,

17:57.993 --> 18:01.872
with almost no water,
no food and no sleep…

18:06.919 --> 18:10.422
I was about to cross the Sanzu River.

18:11.507 --> 18:15.219
I was walking across a bridge,
feeling indescribably blissful.

18:15.928 --> 18:19.598
But my hunger made me dizzy
and fell into the river.

18:21.183 --> 18:24.770
The river was dark and I felt heavy,

18:25.646 --> 18:30.692
but then I felt like I was being massaged
by warm human hands.

18:32.444 --> 18:35.864
I saw something shiny
when I glanced at the bottom of the river,

18:35.948 --> 18:38.617
so I went to grab it
while the hands still massaged me.

18:40.452 --> 18:45.124
Oddly enough, even underwater,
I could smell the shiny stone.

18:49.920 --> 18:52.089
What is this scent?

18:53.173 --> 18:55.300
It smells different
than the Opening Thread.

18:58.137 --> 18:59.304
The left side of my head.

18:59.388 --> 19:00.681
My neck.

19:00.806 --> 19:02.141
Right side of my chest.

19:02.266 --> 19:03.684
The left side of my torso.

19:04.268 --> 19:05.269
My right thigh.

19:05.352 --> 19:06.270
My right shoulder.

19:07.604 --> 19:08.772
Here it comes!

19:17.281 --> 19:19.575
You finally got a hit in, Tanjiro!

19:19.658 --> 19:22.870
Even though it was so feeble
that the doll didn't even flinch,

19:22.953 --> 19:25.289
I'm going to give you some food!

19:26.248 --> 19:30.210
Give me rice balls with pickled plum!
And high-quality, premium green tea!

19:35.382 --> 19:38.135
Delicious!

19:42.055 --> 19:45.350
All right! I can do it!
I can read its movements.

19:46.059 --> 19:47.936
I can see it clearer than before.

19:48.020 --> 19:50.606
And now that my stamina's back,
I can keep up with it!

19:53.400 --> 19:56.987
Now, I can tell by the scent
where he's going to strike.

20:01.491 --> 20:05.078
This scent appears earlier
than the Opening Thread.

20:10.542 --> 20:12.127
All right! I got him!

20:12.211 --> 20:14.171
One strike with all my strength!

20:16.131 --> 20:17.341
But, if it breaks…

20:20.677 --> 20:21.637
Strike!

20:22.346 --> 20:23.680
I don't care if it breaks!

20:24.681 --> 20:26.683
I'll fix it, no matter what!

20:30.020 --> 20:32.606
Tanjiro, you're far too kind.

20:33.190 --> 20:34.983
You must not hesitate now.

20:35.943 --> 20:40.489
I know it's your nature, Tanjiro,
but I don't want you to die!

20:41.740 --> 20:44.451
I want you
to become stronger than everyone else!

20:51.750 --> 20:54.086
Tanjiro! Are you all right?

20:55.712 --> 20:59.424
Sorry, I broke the sword you lent me.

20:59.508 --> 21:01.593
Don't worry about that, I don't mind.

21:10.018 --> 21:11.645
Something's coming out of it!

21:11.728 --> 21:14.189
Kotetsu, something's in there!
What is that thing?

21:14.273 --> 21:16.942
I have no idea either! I swear!

21:24.866 --> 21:27.077
Is that a sword?

21:27.160 --> 21:31.039
It has to be
at least 300 years-old, right?

23:06.093 --> 23:07.052
DEMON SLAYER: SWORDSMITH VILLAGE ARC
NO. 2

23:07.677 --> 23:09.429
That looks good on you, Nezuko.

23:12.974 --> 23:14.309
So, you like it too?

23:15.769 --> 23:18.897
Now, it's time for a Taishō era secret.

23:18.980 --> 23:21.149
It's about Kotetsu,
the swordsmith apprentice.

23:21.233 --> 23:24.486
They say his face
is so similar to the mask he wears,

23:24.569 --> 23:29.533
that it's been suggested
that he doesn't need to wear one at all.

23:29.616 --> 23:34.996
He may have a sharp tongue,
but he's still a sweet boy at heart.

23:36.123 --> 23:40.043
Next up, Episode 3,
"A Sword from Over 300 Years Ago."

23:40.127 --> 23:41.378
It's really hot.

23:41.461 --> 23:43.713
Tanjiro, where are you?

23:45.006 --> 23:46.258
Let's continue training!

23:46.341 --> 23:48.385
If you slack off
after having one good day,

23:48.468 --> 23:50.053
you'll be back where you started.

23:50.137 --> 23:51.221
Perseverance prevails.

23:51.304 --> 23:54.683
Remember The Ant and the Grasshopper?
You're moving at a snail's pace!

23:54.766 --> 23:56.893
Tanjiro, where are you?

23:56.977 --> 23:59.855
-Nezuko, let's run away!
-Tanjiro, where are you?

23:59.938 --> 24:01.022
TO BE CONTINUED
